00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:35.060
<b>Osorezan, one of the three great places of Japan,
resides in the northernmost tip of Honshu island.</b>

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:43.480
<b>It's a desolate place, cloaked in steam and
sulfurous fumes that stream from volcanic fumaroles.</b>

00:13:44.570 --> 00:13:50.450
<b>Nearby, a hushed silence hangs over a caldera
like with a beach of the color of old bones.</b>

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:56.160
<b>People saw death in these under-worldly
landscapes that were neither heaven nor hell.</b>

00:13:56.460 --> 00:14:02.630
<b>They called it Osorezan. It became a
place for the living to mourn the dead.</b>

00:13:56.460 --> 00:14:02.630
TL note: Osorezan means "The mountain of fear"

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:06.670
<b>Ghosts with nowhere
else to go end up there.</b>

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:11.180
<b>The mountain is a bridge
between this world and the next</b>

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:14.560
<b>It breaks my heart.</b>

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:20.020
<b>S-sounds kinda scary.</b>

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:22.110
<b>That’s where I'm gonna meet my wife?</b>

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:25.690
<b>Hahaha, having second thoughts?</b>

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:30.950
<b>No Asakura could possibly fear ghosts.</b>

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:35.910
<b>B-but you just said
you'd rather not go there!</b>

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:39.300
<b>How do you know all this
if you've never been there?</b>

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:40.560
<b>I read about it.</b>

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:41.680
<b>Pamphlet?!</b>

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:44.710
<b>But there's nothing like
seeing a thing for oneself...</b>

